# Changelog

All notable changes to hyprtk-merged (the unified dotfiles installer) are
documented in this file. Dates are in YYYY-MM-DD format.

## [Unreleased] - 2026-09-17

### Added

- **doas-only systems (Alpine).** The installer was hard-wired to `sudo`.
  `installer/scripts/pkgmanager.sh` now exports a `sudo`→`doas` compatibility
  function and `hyprtk_run_root` falls back to `doas`; `1-install.sh`'s
  `_sudo_bootstrap` gained a doas branch that authenticates once and installs a
  temporary `/etc/doas.d/99-hyprtk-install.conf` nopass drop-in (removed on
  exit — doas.d is last-match, so it must sort last). Validated on Alpine with
  `sudo` removed entirely.

### Fixed

- **Alpine: SDDM would not launch and tty sessions died with
  "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is not set".** Root cause: busybox mdev never applies the
  elogind udev rules, so the DRM card is not tagged `master-of-seat`
  (`CanGraphical=no`), and no OpenRC services were enabled. `system.sh` now
  installs eudev and enables `udev`/`udev-trigger`/`udev-settle`/
  `udev-postmount` (removing mdev from sysinit), enables `dbus`/`elogind`/`sddm`
  at boot, and writes an `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` fallback to
  `/etc/profile.d/`. Verified: SDDM launches its greeter at boot and a session
  gets `/run/user/<uid>`.
- **Alpine: the bundled `gum` is a glibc binary** that cannot execute on musl,
  and the dotfiles symlink it into `~/.local/bin` (on PATH), so `command -v gum`
  resolved to the broken copy and the installer aborted at the first prompt.
  `check_gum` now runs every candidate and falls back to a working system gum.
- **Alpine: Sugar-Candy silently fell back to SDDM's built-in theme** (Qt6 SDDM
  looked for the missing Qt5 greeter). `sddmgrub.sh` now appends `QtVersion=6`
  to the theme metadata alongside the QML import patch.
- **Alpine install steps**: the root Papirus icon install runs via `sudo` with
  `DESTDIR`; `/root/.cache` is created before copying the root wallpaper;
  bluetooth and samba use OpenRC (`rc-service`/`rc-update`) where systemd is
  absent; cockpit is skipped with a warning on non-systemd systems.
- **Re-runs**: the oh-my-zsh upstream installer is skipped when `~/.oh-my-zsh`
  already exists (it exits non-zero on an existing install).

## [Unreleased] - 2026-09-14

### Added

- **Cross-distro package audit (2026-09-17).** New
  `installer/scripts/verify/package-audit.sh` resolves every native name the
  installer requests (via each `hypr/packages/*.sh --list` plus the vendored
  bar's DEPS/EXTRAS) against live repository metadata in throwaway containers
  and emits a per-name TSV; `installer/scripts/verify/package-audit-html.py`
  renders it to `output.html` (per-distro tables + an action list).
  Result across pacman/apt(×5)/dnf/zypper/xbps/apk: **1165 in-repo, 16 AUR,
  78 allow-listed gaps, 0 unexpected**. The actionable gaps are the extra repos
  the installer does not add yet — Fedora NVIDIA/mesa need **RPMFusion**,
  Debian needs **non-free**, Void/Alpine need their **nonfree** repos — plus
  genuinely unpackaged extras (cockpit on Void/Alpine, cliphist on Alpine,
  hyprsunset on Void, polkit-gnome on Fedora, gvfs-nfs on Void).
  `manual_package_installs.sh` lost its `hyprtk-pkglist` marker and is excluded
  from the audit/matrix, so it no longer counts toward the installer surface.
- **Extra repositories + source fallbacks (2026-09-17).** The audit's "Extra
  (TODO)" gaps are now wired up:
  - `pkgmanager.sh` gained `hyprtk_enable_extra_repos`, run by the new
    `installer/scripts/enable-extra-repos.sh` before the core packages:
    **RPMFusion** free+nonfree on Fedora, **contrib/non-free/non-free-firmware**
    on Debian, and the **nonfree** repo on Void. Alpine ships no nonfree repo,
    so its NVIDIA/unrar genuinely cannot be installed.
  - Fedora AMD now requests `mesa-va-drivers-freeworld` (RPMFusion) instead of
    the non-existent `mesa-va-drivers`.
  - `polkit-gnome` → `mate-polkit` on Fedora and Debian 13, with a new
    `hypr/scripts/polkit-agent.sh` that launches whichever agent exists (the
    session previously called the polkit-gnome path unconditionally).
  - `freerdp3-x11` → `freerdp2-x11` fallback on Debian 12; dropped `gvfs-nfs`
    on Void (its gvfs is monolithic).
  - `srcapps-install.sh` now builds `cliphist` (go), `eza` (cargo), `ipp-usb`
    (go + libusb + avahi, with its udev rule), and — via a from-source build of
    the **Hyprland library chain** (`hyprland-protocols`, `hyprutils`,
    `hyprwayland-scanner`, plus `hyprlang` for sunset) — `hyprpicker` on Alpine
    and `hyprsunset` on Void, where neither the apps nor their libraries are
    packaged. Both chains were verified to build and run in their target distro.
  - After the change the audit's **Extra (TODO) column is 0 on every family**,
    and the buildable gap is closed. The 7 remaining gaps are not buildable in
    practice:
    - Alpine: `nvidia`/`nvidia-settings` (binary-only driver), `unrar`
      (non-free), `nss-mdns` (**glibc-only** — needs `<nss.h>`, cannot build
      against musl), `cockpit` (large Python/JS app).
    - Void: `cockpit`, `nvidia-settings` (not packaged).

- **Fedora install fixes (2026-09-17, found on a live F44 Xfce VM).**
  - `hyprland.sh` enables a Hyprland COPR on Fedora/RHEL
    (`lionheartp/Hyprland`, falling back to `solopasha/hyprland`). Hyprland is
    not in the Fedora base repos, so it silently never installed and the
    compositor could not start from a TTY. The COPR also supplies `nwg-look`
    and `hyprsunset`.
  - `sddmgrub.sh` fixes two SDDM 0.21 faults: the Wayland greeter died on
    Fedora (now `DisplayServer=x11` off-Arch via a `zz-` drop-in, keeping Arch's
    Wayland path) and the Qt5 Sugar-Candy theme failed to load under Qt6 (QML
    imports rewritten to `Qt5Compat.GraphicalEffects` / versionless
    `QtQuick.VirtualKeyboard`, with the Qt5-compat QML modules installed).
  - `fonts.sh` decided on directory existence rather than content, so an empty
    `~/.local/share/fonts` (seen on openSUSE) skipped the clone; it now clones
    into an empty dir and `git pull`s an existing clone.
  - `awww-install.sh` installs the distro Rust toolchain when it meets the MSRV,
    falling back to rustup only when it does not — avoiding the rustup download
    on Fedora/openSUSE.
  - `manual_package_installs.sh` removed from the core loop: it is a manual,
    opt-in helper, not part of `1-install.sh`.
- **More Fedora fixes (2026-09-17, second pass on the same VM).**
  - `installer/standalone/awww` (the wrapper that lands on PATH) hardcoded
    `REAL_AWW=/usr/bin/awww`, so on Fedora — where awww is a `/usr/local/bin`
    source build — every wallpaper change failed silently. It now resolves the
    real awww/swww at runtime, and both it and `awww-wrapper.sh` pick the image
    argument that names a real file (flags may follow the path).
  - `hypr/scripts/wallpaper-colors.sh` no longer calls `awww img`: the wrapper
    already applied the wallpaper before invoking it, so the call made the
    wrapper recurse on every change.
  - `1-install.sh` runs `chsh` with an explicit target user (`SUDO_USER`); with
    no user argument `chsh` under sudo changed **root**'s shell, so the user's
    login shell stayed bash. zsh is also ensured present in `/etc/shells`.
  - New `configs/swaylock-plain/config` and a capability check in `1-install.sh`
    (`swaylock --help | grep -- --effect-pixelate`): plain swaylock rejects the
    effects-only options (`clock`, `timestr`, `datestr`, `fade-in`,
    `effect-pixelate`, bare `indicator`) and refused to lock, so non-effects
    builds now get the plain variant while Arch keeps the effects config.
  - New `installer/scripts/xdg-autostart-cleanup.sh`, run during configuration:
    uwsm sessions run `systemd-xdg-autostart`, so distro defaults for another
    desktop also launch under Hyprland. Fedora Xfce's `dnfdragora-updater`
    crashes there (python SIGABRT) and pops an ABRT "Oops!" dialog at every
    login; it is suppressed per-user with a `Hidden=true` override.
- **Brave + preferred-app defaults (2026-09-17).**
  - `webtools.sh` installs Brave on Fedora/RHEL and openSUSE from Brave's
    official RPM repo (`brave-browser`), matching the existing apt-repo and AUR
    paths. Previously Brave only installed on Arch (AUR) and Debian/Ubuntu, so
    the Fedora/openSUSE installs had no browser.
  - New `installer/scripts/set-default-apps.sh` (run during dotfiles setup) and
    `TERMINAL=alacritty` in `hypr/environment.lua`. hyprtk-bar's quick links
    resolve "System default" from XDG (`xdg-mime`/`xdg-settings`) and `$TERMINAL`;
    a fresh distro pointed those at its own apps (Fedora: `kitty` for
    `inode/directory`, `firefox` for web, `xdg-terminal-exec` for the terminal),
    so the terminal/file-manager/browser links never showed alacritty/thunar/brave.

- **Container package-name matrix (T1).** New
  `installer/scripts/verify/container-matrix.sh` resolves every native name from
  `hypr/packages/*.sh` + the vendored bar in a throwaway rootless-podman
  container per family (pacman/apt/dnf/zypper/xbps/apk; apt on Debian 12/13 and
  Ubuntu 24.04/26.04) without installing. Arch misses are checked against the
  AUR; expected gaps live in `container-matrix.allow`. Result: **1059
  resolvable, 21 AUR, 67 allow-listed, 0 unexpected** (Ubuntu 26.04 alone leaves
  just `brave-browser`, `hyprsunset`, `nvidia-driver`). Renames this surfaced:
  - pacman: `ttf-font-awesome` → `otf-font-awesome`; `exa` → `eza`; resolver now
    accepts pacman **groups** (`xfce4`, `xfce4-goodies`).
  - dnf: `ffmpeg` → `ffmpeg-free`; `intel-media-driver` →
    `libva-intel-media-driver`; `fontawesome-fonts` → `fontawesome-fonts-all`;
    `xorg-x11-server-utils` → `xhost`.
  - zypper: `gtk-layer-shell` → `libgtk-layer-shell0`, `gtk4-layer-shell` →
    `libgtk4-layer-shell0`; dropped `xfce4-goodies`.
  - xbps: `fira-code` → `font-firacode`, `font-manager` → `fontmanager`,
    `mesa-va-drivers` → `mesa-vaapi`, `xfce4-goodies` → `xfce4-plugins`.
  - apk: `fira-code` → `font-fira-code-nerd`, `mesa-vulkan-radeon` →
    `mesa-vulkan-ati`, `xfce4-plugins` → `xfce4-panel`.
  - `graphics-card.sh` gained a `--list` guard (it carried package lists but was
    never enumerable); `3dprinting.sh` `--list` no longer emits its AUR slicers
    on non-Arch families.
- **Full installer dry-run in containers (T2).** New
  `installer/scripts/verify/container-dryrun.sh` runs the whole installer in a
  throwaway container per family/variant (arch, Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 24.04/26.04,
  Fedora, openSUSE, Void, Alpine; Gentoo/NixOS advisory) with every mutating
  command + the family PM stubbed and `HYPRTK_DRYRUN=1`. Result: **12/12** (ten
  installable rows — Arch, Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 24.04/26.04, **Linux Mint 22.3**,
  Fedora, openSUSE, Void, Alpine — complete cleanly; Gentoo/NixOS complete with
  package deps skipped).
- **Source-built apps (`srcapps-install.sh`).** Apps absent from a family's
  archives are now built from source / installed from upstream when the native
  package is missing: **gtk4-layer-shell** (meson `v1.3.0`; also creates
  `/usr/lib/libgtk4-layer-shell.so` for matuwall's `LD_PRELOAD`), **swappy**
  (meson `v1.8.0`; `grim.sh`'s editor), **nwg-look** (`go build` `v1.1.1`) and
  **starship** (upstream installer `v1.26.0`). Idempotent, non-fatal and
  `HYPRTK_DRYRUN`-aware; per-family build-dep maps. Verified with real builds in
  Linux Mint 22.3, Alpine and Fedora.
- **Linux Mint 22.3 (Ubuntu-24.04 family) support.** Added Mint to the T1 matrix
  and the T2 dry-run. New `pkgmanager.sh` helpers — `hyprtk_apt_add_ppa`,
  `hyprtk_ubuntu_codename`, `hyprtk_is_ubuntu_family` — add a Launchpad PPA by
  explicit keyring + `sources.list.d` (no `add-apt-repository`/Launchpad API).
  `hyprland.sh` uses it for **cppiber/hyprland** (Hyprland `0.56.2` +
  hyprpicker/hyprsunset) and `terminaltools.sh` for **zhangsongcui3371/fastfetch**
  (noble has no `fastfetch`).
- **awww source build validated in containers (T3).** Ubuntu 24.04, Fedora and
  openSUSE Tumbleweed build `awww 0.12.1`. Debian 12 cannot (libwayland 1.21 <
  the required 1.22); `awww-install.sh` now checks `wayland-client` up front and
  fails fast with a clear reason instead of downloading rustup first.
- **Package-name audit.** Corrected package names that silently failed to
  install (findings: Ubuntu 26.04 VM + Fedora/openSUSE/Void repo metadata):
  - **apt (Ubuntu 26.04)** — `gtk-layer-shell` → `libgtk-layer-shell0`,
    `gtk4-layer-shell` → `libgtk4-layer-shell0`, `cups-pdf` →
    `printer-driver-cups-pdf`, `fonts-fira-code` → `fonts-firacode`,
    `freerdp2-x11` → `freerdp3-x11`; removed `mission-center` and
    `thunar-shares-plugin` (not packaged on Ubuntu). All apt lists now resolve
    cleanly (`apt-get install -s`).
  - **Fedora** — `p7zip` → `7zip`, `thunar` → `Thunar`, `libusb` → `libusb1`;
    dropped `thunar-shares-plugin`, `mission-center`, `xfce4-goodies`.
  - **openSUSE** — `micro` → `micro-editor`, dropped `mission-center`; bar extras
    `pipewire-pulse` → `pipewire-pulseaudio`, `libnotify` → `libnotify-tools`.
  - **Void** — `thunar` → `Thunar`, dropped `mission-center`.
  - **bar** — `EXTRAS[apt]` `libnotify`/`policykit-1` → `libnotify-bin`/
    `polkitd pkexec`.
- **`manual_package_installs.sh` and `3dprinting.sh` wired into the core loop**
  (both were never invoked, so their packages/extras silently never installed).
- **Multi-distro install — hyprtk now installs on any Linux distribution.**
  New `installer/scripts/pkgmanager.sh` detects the host package manager
  (pacman/apt/dnf/zypper/xbps/apk/emerge/nix) and provides
  `pkg_install`/`pkg_remove`/`pkg_is_installed`/`aur_install` wrappers. Every
  `hypr/packages/*.sh` script now carries an exhaustive per-family package list
  (Arch, Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora/RHEL, openSUSE, Void, Alpine) with an Arch AUR
  list, and supports `--list` for the installer's spinner preview.
- `1-install.sh` detects Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora/RHEL, openSUSE, Void, Alpine,
  Gentoo and NixOS (via `ID`/`ID_LIKE`) in addition to the 11 Arch-based
  distros, with a family/manager readout and an expanded manual-selection menu.
- `PORTABILITY.md` documenting the family matrix, Arch-only features and
  per-family gotchas.
- **Cross-distro awww** — new `installer/scripts/awww-install.sh` acquires the
  wallpaper daemon without the AUR: native `swww` on Void/Alpine, otherwise a
  pinned source build of `LGFae/awww` (`v0.12.1`, GPL-3) via `cargo build
  --release`, with rustup bootstrapped when the distro's `rustc` is older than
  upstream's 1.89 MSRV. Binaries install to `/usr/local/bin` with `swww`
  compatibility symlinks; `1-install.sh` runs it (before the wrapper) and the
  step is non-fatal with manual instructions when no route exists.
- **Hyprland ≥ 0.55 on Ubuntu** — the dotfiles' config is Lua-based, which
  Hyprland only reads from 0.55 onward, but Ubuntu 26.04's archive ships 0.53.3
  (which silently generates a stock `hyprland.conf` and ignores the Lua config).
  `hypr/packages/hyprland.sh` now adds the community `cppiber/hyprland` PPA
  (0.56.2 for resolute) on Ubuntu and installs with
  `-o Dpkg::Options::=--force-overwrite` to clear the PPA's overlapping file
  lists with the archive `libhyprcursor0`/`libudis86-0`. Debian (no PPA) warns
  and keeps the archive package.

### Changed

- The AUR helper (`yay`) step runs only on Arch; other families skip it.
- `library.sh` delegates to the abstraction while keeping the historic
  `_installPackages*`/`_isInstalled*` names; the pkgmanager primitives are
  exported for the installer's `bash -c` spinner subshells.
- Package scripts and misc helpers are invoked with `bash` explicitly (they use
  arrays), not `sh`.
- Misc system scripts are now PM-aware: `rm-dm-managers.sh`, `cleanup.sh`,
  `installupdates.sh`, `updates.sh` (distro-agnostic), `snapper-setup.sh`,
  `vmware-setup.sh`, `qemu-virt-setup.sh`, `appimage-setup.sh`.
- `graphics-card.sh` installs the Intel/AMD/NVIDIA stack per family and guards
  the `mkinitcpio`/GRUB steps; `sddmgrub.sh`/`sddm-check.sh` use repo-relative
  paths and `hyprtk_run_root`.
- Root `.bashrc`'s `update` alias is now a distro-aware function.

### Fixed

- **Installer "went stale" in the apt package phase on Linux Mint / Ubuntu.**
  The `system.sh` batch (the largest apt step) could hang invisibly inside the
  `gum spin`: Mint's background updaters (mintupdate, unattended-upgrades,
  packagekit, apt-daily) can hold the dpkg/apt lock, and debconf/needrestart can
  prompt. `pkgmanager.sh` now routes every apt call through an `_apt` wrapper
  (`DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive`, `NEEDRESTART_MODE=a`,
  `-o DPkg::Lock::Timeout=600`, dpkg `--force-confdef/--force-confold`), and
  `1-install.sh` calls a new `hyprtk_apt_wait_lock` before the core package loop
  that waits visibly (flock poll, 5s steps, 10-min cap) and announces a held
  lock. `hyprland.sh`/`webtools.sh` use `_apt` too.
- **Void Linux: Hyprland availability documented.** Void does not package
  `hyprland` (a packaging-philosophy conflict). `hypr/packages/hyprland.sh` now
  prints the community-repo steps (void-land/hyprland-void-packages,
  `xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland`) when the compositor is still missing on xbps, and
  `PORTABILITY.md` marks Void as ⚠️ community-repo (and Fedora as ⚠️ COPR). The
  installer does not add a third-party repo by itself.
- **Choosing "Nvidia" in `graphics-card.sh` installed the AMD stack.** The menu
  `case` arms were ordered `1)` / `2|*)` / `3)`, so the `*` catch-all matched `3`
  and the Nvidia arm was unreachable. Reordered to `1)` / `3)` / `2|*)`, and the
  apt Nvidia arm gained a **versioned fallback** — Ubuntu/Mint ship no generic
  `nvidia-driver` meta, so the newest `nvidia-driver-5xx` is selected instead
  (Mint 22.3 → `nvidia-driver-610`).
- **Hyprland (and hyprpicker/hyprsunset) never installed on Ubuntu 24.04 /
  Linux Mint 22.3.** `add-apt-repository -y ppa:cppiber/hyprland` fails there
  ("This codename isn't currently supported") — it needs a reachable Launchpad
  API and `software-properties-common`. The PPA *does* publish `noble`; it is now
  added by explicit keyring + source (`hyprtk_apt_add_ppa`), with
  `add-apt-repository` only as a fallback. This restores the core compositor.
- **os-release single-quoted values broke distro detection.** `1-install.sh`
  `_detect_distro` (and `hyprland.sh`'s `_hyprtk_is_ubuntu`) stripped only double
  quotes, so Gentoo's `ID='gentoo'` was not recognised. Both now strip `"` and
  `'`. Found by the T2 container dry-run on Gentoo.
- **Vendored bar `DEPS[zypper]` used non-existent openSUSE packages**
  (`typelib-1_0-cairo-1_0`, `typelib-1_0-xlib-2_0`). Fixed upstream in
  `hyprtk-bar` (→ `girepository-1_0`, which provides both `cairo-1.0` and
  `xlib-2.0` typelibs) and re-vendored into `installer/hyprtk-bar/` here and in
  `hyprtk-merged`. Verified: openSUSE resolves 118/118 and the bar's
  `--no-extras` install + Gtk/GtkLayerShell import passes.
- `hyprviz.sh` builds in a dedicated dir and skips cleanly off Arch.
- `fonts.sh`/`wallpapers.sh`/`matuwall.sh` resolve repo-relative asset paths and
  use `python3`.
- **awww wrapper no longer assumes `/usr/bin/awww`** — `awww-wrapper.sh`
  resolves the real binary (AUR `/usr/bin`, source-build `/usr/local/bin`, or a
  Void/Alpine `swww`) instead of hardcoding the AUR path, so it no longer fails
  on non-Arch installs where awww was never installed.

## [Unreleased] - 2026-09-07

### Changed

- **pywal16 bundled — the AUR dependency is gone** — pywal16 is now vendored
  inside hyprtk-bar (`installer/hyprtk-bar/vendor/pywal16/`; MIT, v3.8.15,
  commit `a04c3e3`) and exposed as `wal` (`venv/bin/wal`, symlinked into
  `~/.local/bin`). `1-install.sh` provisions it early with
  `installer/hyprtk-bar/install.sh --wal-only`, replacing the
  `yay -S python-pywal16-git` step; `python-pywal16-git` was removed from the
  AUR extras. The bar and its scripts resolve the bundled `wal` first
  (`HYPRTK_WAL` → `~/.local/bin` → beside-install → PATH), so a stale system
  `wal` cannot shadow it. See `installer/hyprtk-bar/BUNDLING.md` and
  `installer/hyprtk-bar/vendor/pywal16/VENDOR.md`.
- **hyprtk-bar settings window single border** — the floating bar-settings
  window previously showed a double border: Hyprland drew its own compositor
  window border around the plain `Gtk.Window` on top of the CSS `.popup-box`
  border. Added `border_size = 0` to the `windowrule-bar-settings` rule so only
  the CSS animated border shows, matching the layer-shell dialogs.
- **hyprtk-bar border animation mirrors Hyprland** — vendored hyprtk-bar now
  animates its pill border at the same pace as Hyprland's `borderangle`
  (speed = duration in ds, `speed * 100` ms) and exposes an Animations tab
  (Low / High / Custom; custom speed independent of Hyprland).
- **hyprtk-bar GPU page supports Intel + NVIDIA** — auto-picks the primary GPU
  and reads amdgpu sysfs / `nvidia-smi` / Intel i915+xe sysfs (vendored).
- hyprtk-menu theming shares the bar's theme model (pywal / waybar / manual).

## [0.2.0] - 2026-09-05

### Changed

- **Waybar + dunst fully removed** — replaced by the bundled **hyprtk-bar**
  (taskbar, system tray, and built-in notification center all in one app).
  `configs/waybar` (incl. all themes), `configs/dunst`, and the waybar-only
  color script were deleted; packages, keybindings, wal/wallpaper script
  launches, RTMIN signals and dunstrc copies removed.
- hyprtk-bar, hyprtk-menu, hyprtk-arc-menu and theme-gui vendored into
  `installer/` and wired into `1-install.sh`; gtk3 + desktop-file-utils added
  to the hyprland package deps.
- Rofi variants aligned with the bar theme: accent switched to pywal color5,
  aero variant made pywal-aware, `hyprtk-glass` variant added; the bar syncs
  the rofi variant on every re-theme.
- hyprtk-bar + hyprtk-arc-menu autostart fixed (Hyprland autostart PATH lacks
  `~/.local/bin` — use absolute paths).
- SDDM/GRUB module (theme-gui) uses pkexec; theme-gui standalone wrapper path
  fixed.

## [0.1.0] - 2026-08-13

### Added

- **Unified 11-distro installer** — one `1-install.sh` covering Arch, ArchBang,
  Archcraft, ArchMan, Bluestar, CachyOS, EndeavourOS, Garuda, Kiro, Manjaro and
  RebornOS, with per-distro hooks in `installer/steps/` (os-release install,
  boot splash, grub wallpaper/updater, wal re-init, hypr-config backup,
  sudoers).
- New 4-category tree layout: `assets/` (fonts, wallpapers, themes, papirus
  icons, splash, screenshots), `configs/` (all app configs + root),
  `hypr/` (Hyprland lua config) and `installer/` (os-release variants, scripts,
  standalone gum, steps). Per-distro overlays under `distro/<name>/`.
- Gum TUI installer with distro auto-detection (`/etc/os-release`), standalone
  gum binary, `install.log` logging, and dependency audit.
- Verification suite: `installer/scripts/verify/` — completeness, reference
  audit, installer audit, dry-run, and a full end-to-end installer dry-run
  harness (sandboxed `$HOME`, all system-mutating commands stubbed, per-distro
  fake os-release).

### Changed

- Merged the 11 source distro trees into one canonical tree (arch-dots is the
  canonical base; other trees are diff-generated overlays).
- os-release ×11 + fastfetch ASCII logos for every distro.

### Removed

- Separate per-distro repos: everything is merged into a single `dotfiles`
